{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DocStore","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:6Yorkie8DocStoreP","symbolKind":"protocol","title":"DocStore","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DocStore"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DocStore","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is deliberately a snapshot plus an append-only change log rather than one opaque"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"blob. Re-serializing the whole document on every edit costs time proportional to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document – hundreds of milliseconds on a large one – and a document is at its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"largest while it is being edited, which is exactly when the writes happen. Appending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs the size of one change, which does not grow with the document at all."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The interface stays byte-oriented and async so a durable backend can implement it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without the client knowing which storage it talks to, and so a backend is free to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compress or encrypt what it is handed. The default "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/MemoryDocStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","t